1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,814
Characters, actions, places, occupations, and events in this series are fictional and created for entertainment purposes only.

2
00:00:06,814 --> 00:00:11,096
They are not intended to urge or promote any behavior in the series.

3
00:00:11,096 --> 00:00:13,105
Viewer discretion is advised.

4
00:00:13,105 --> 00:00:13,809
Is this the real you?

5
00:00:13,809 --> 00:00:15,451
I apologize on behalf of the illusions.

6
00:00:15,451 --> 00:00:16,087
What does that mean?

7
00:00:16,087 --> 00:00:17,547
It means you miss me, P’Niran.

8
00:00:17,547 --> 00:00:18,644
My name’s not even on that.

9
00:00:18,644 --> 00:00:19,874
How would I know you’re cheering me on?

10
00:00:19,874 --> 00:00:21,942
I wouldn’t cheer for anyone else but you.

11
00:00:21,942 --> 00:00:23,480
I know how much you love astronomy and space.

12
00:00:23,480 --> 00:00:25,226
You can’t miss looking for aliens.

13
00:00:25,844 --> 00:00:27,054
Did you know?

14
00:00:27,054 --> 00:00:30,273
You’re like a newly formed star in the Small Magellanic Cloud.

15
00:00:30,273 --> 00:00:31,897
What about it?

16
00:00:32,141 --> 00:00:33,003
It’s cute.

17
00:01:39,502 --> 00:01:40,228
Hey.

18
00:01:40,397 --> 00:01:41,147
Where are you going?

19
00:01:41,353 --> 00:01:42,445
It’s not even 7 a.m. yet.

20
00:01:44,449 --> 00:01:45,339
I’m going to a volunteer camp.

21
00:01:45,545 --> 00:01:46,408
The bus leaves at 8.

22
00:01:47,270 --> 00:01:48,160
Well…

23
00:01:48,947 --> 00:01:50,801
You’re wasting time doing stuff like this.

24
00:01:51,176 --> 00:01:53,025
Are you really quitting judo?

25
00:01:56,023 --> 00:01:57,816
You don’t even know
why I have to go to the camp.

26
00:01:58,828 --> 00:02:00,548
Have you ever told me anything?

27
00:02:01,640 --> 00:02:03,731
I always have to hear your stories
from someone else.

28
00:02:06,691 --> 00:02:08,780
No one else’s kid is like this.

29
00:02:14,101 --> 00:02:15,923
No one else’s dad is like this either.

30
00:02:17,384 --> 00:02:20,098
Even now, you’re still comparing me
to other families’ kids.

31
00:02:22,178 --> 00:02:23,282
Wait, Niran.

32
00:02:46,848 --> 00:02:47,776
Have you been waiting long?

33
00:02:48,900 --> 00:02:50,094
I just got out of the house.

34
00:02:50,581 --> 00:02:51,970
Hey, you don’t have to.

35
00:02:51,970 --> 00:02:52,619
I’ve got it.

36
00:03:06,719 --> 00:03:07,411
Hello.

37
00:03:09,828 --> 00:03:11,085
You’re Niran, right?

38
00:03:11,422 --> 00:03:13,022
Hello, I’m Niran.

39
00:03:13,266 --> 00:03:14,697
Sorry to trouble you, P’Cheewin.

40
00:03:14,903 --> 00:03:16,036
Not at all.

41
00:03:16,440 --> 00:03:18,279
I have to drop Cheewa off anyway.

42
00:03:19,665 --> 00:03:20,377
Come on.

43
00:03:20,752 --> 00:03:21,810
Let me put your bag in the car.

44
00:03:22,223 --> 00:03:22,898
Thank you.

45
00:03:28,912 --> 00:03:30,259
Are you okay?

46
00:03:31,364 --> 00:03:32,192
Who’s not okay?

47
00:03:32,192 --> 00:03:33,890
You, P’Niran.
Why do you look tense?

48
00:03:34,358 --> 00:03:35,659
My brother is kind.

49
00:03:38,020 --> 00:03:41,764
It’s just that this feels weird.

50
00:03:42,513 --> 00:03:43,893
You and I aren’t even close yet,

51
00:03:44,642 --> 00:03:46,682
and I’m already bothering your brother
to give me a ride to school.

52
00:03:47,488 --> 00:03:49,334
I’ll try to get close to you.

53
00:03:49,859 --> 00:03:51,067
Let’s get in the car.

54
00:03:55,320 --> 00:03:56,404
Did you just grab my arm?

55
00:03:56,685 --> 00:03:57,597
Get in.

56
00:04:13,315 --> 00:04:14,974
What time did you get up today, Niran?

57
00:04:16,510 --> 00:04:18,298
I usually wake up very early.

58
00:04:18,635 --> 00:04:19,348
Really?

59
00:04:19,891 --> 00:04:21,110
Wow, that’s great.

60
00:04:21,710 --> 00:04:25,031
I had to wake Cheewa up a couple of times
before he finally got up.

61
00:04:25,218 --> 00:04:26,084
Oh.

62
00:04:26,534 --> 00:04:29,833
I’m an athlete.

63
00:04:29,833 --> 00:04:32,233
When training gets intense,
I have to get up really early.

64
00:04:32,514 --> 00:04:34,673
Oh, you’re an athlete?

65
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:35,828
What do you do?

66
00:04:35,828 --> 00:04:36,723
Judo.

67
00:04:36,910 --> 00:04:37,530
Oh.

68
00:04:37,530 --> 00:04:39,886
P’Niran tried out for the national team.

69
00:04:40,317 --> 00:04:42,717
Everyone at school knows him.

70
00:04:43,167 --> 00:04:44,584
Cheewa, you talk too much.

71
00:04:47,713 --> 00:04:49,063
Ask Cheewa to join you sometime.

72
00:04:49,325 --> 00:04:51,601
All he does is read.

73
00:04:51,713 --> 00:04:53,086
He’s practically a bookworm.

74
00:04:53,386 --> 00:04:55,268
Who knows
when he’s going to explore space?

75
00:04:56,748 --> 00:05:00,270
P’Cheewin, did you know
how long a scientist needs to prepare

76
00:05:00,270 --> 00:05:02,001
before they go on an expedition?

77
00:05:02,638 --> 00:05:06,536
I study eight hours a day.

78
00:05:06,536 --> 00:05:07,460
Five days a week.

79
00:05:07,460 --> 00:05:08,128
I’m not—

80
00:05:08,128 --> 00:05:09,505
Alright, fine.

81
00:05:09,505 --> 00:05:10,651
I know.

82
00:05:11,325 --> 00:05:12,346
I’m just being sarcastic.

83
00:05:21,264 --> 00:05:24,796
Niran, please take care of my little brother.

84
00:05:26,201 --> 00:05:28,775
He doesn't introduce me
to his new friends very often.

85
00:05:29,730 --> 00:05:33,379
At first, I was surprised
he asked me to pick you up.

86
00:05:36,583 --> 00:05:37,536
Gladly, P’Cheewin.

87
00:05:37,536 --> 00:05:39,953
If your brother misbehaves, I’ll handle him.

88
00:05:43,475 --> 00:05:44,827
I’ll leave it to you then.

89
00:05:45,595 --> 00:05:46,366
I’m off.

90
00:05:46,478 --> 00:05:47,693
Have a safe trip.

91
00:05:47,693 --> 00:05:48,403
Bye.

92
00:05:48,647 --> 00:05:49,531
- Bye.
- Bye.

93
00:05:58,500 --> 00:05:59,509
We’re not friends.

94
00:05:59,509 --> 00:06:00,204
Huh?

95
00:06:01,553 --> 00:06:03,082
P’Cheewin just said

96
00:06:03,307 --> 00:06:04,561
you’re my new friend.

97
00:06:05,179 --> 00:06:06,729
I don’t want to be your friend.

98
00:06:06,729 --> 00:06:07,229
I want to date—

99
00:06:07,229 --> 00:06:08,948
I think we should go.

100
00:06:08,948 --> 00:06:10,008
The bus is about to leave.

101
00:06:10,252 --> 00:06:10,938
Yeah.

102
00:06:11,538 --> 00:06:13,126
Is that Hem?

103
00:06:13,126 --> 00:06:14,576
Cheewa, look. Is that Hem?

104
00:06:14,576 --> 00:06:16,206
Oh, it’s not. It’s Thara.

105
00:06:16,318 --> 00:06:18,873
We have a real chance of seeing Orion
if the sky is clear.

106
00:06:20,728 --> 00:06:21,698
We do,

107
00:06:21,829 --> 00:06:23,265
but we probably won’t see the belt.

108
00:06:23,471 --> 00:06:24,804
It’s not dark enough.

109
00:06:25,628 --> 00:06:28,167
At least we’ll get to see our beloved
tonight for sure.

110
00:06:28,692 --> 00:06:29,999
- The Scorpion.
- The Scorpion.

111
00:06:30,973 --> 00:06:31,636
Yes.

112
00:06:31,636 --> 00:06:32,760
What scorpion?

113
00:06:34,783 --> 00:06:35,696
I have no idea.

114
00:06:37,270 --> 00:06:37,813
There they are.

115
00:06:37,907 --> 00:06:39,207
What time is it now?

116
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:40,818
Took you guys long enough.

117
00:06:40,818 --> 00:06:41,510
Mm.

118
00:06:43,402 --> 00:06:44,888
You brought a guitar?

119
00:06:45,375 --> 00:06:47,188
Are you going to strum it
while playing in the sea?

120
00:06:47,394 --> 00:06:48,838
Strum your lips.

121
00:06:50,112 --> 00:06:50,918
Why are you so late?

122
00:06:51,218 --> 00:06:52,240
You said you’d arrive early.

123
00:06:52,240 --> 00:06:53,643
It’s Newton’s fault.

124
00:06:53,830 --> 00:06:54,790
We ran into him.

125
00:06:55,000 --> 00:06:57,653
He was busy shopping.

126
00:06:57,897 --> 00:06:58,883
That’s not true.

127
00:06:58,883 --> 00:07:01,139
I got here a long time ago.
I just stopped to buy some stuff.

128
00:07:01,139 --> 00:07:04,115
Then I ran into these two,
and they held me up.

129
00:07:04,696 --> 00:07:06,554
They wanted to go to the grocery store
in front of the school.

130
00:07:07,004 --> 00:07:07,939
P’Hem bought—

131
00:07:07,939 --> 00:07:08,893
Hey.

132
00:07:09,043 --> 00:07:09,762
Hey.

133
00:07:09,762 --> 00:07:10,541
Calm down.

134
00:07:10,991 --> 00:07:12,597
It’s me. I was just joking.

135
00:07:14,002 --> 00:07:14,663
Okay?

136
00:07:18,016 --> 00:07:18,731
Yeah.

137
00:07:18,825 --> 00:07:19,791
Fine, I was the one who was slow.

138
00:07:20,372 --> 00:07:21,010
I’m sorry.

139
00:07:21,422 --> 00:07:22,524
I couldn’t find what I wanted.

140
00:07:22,805 --> 00:07:23,886
What were you looking for?

141
00:07:24,055 --> 00:07:25,007
Not just the guitar?

142
00:07:25,007 --> 00:07:25,935
You want to play the drums too?

143
00:07:25,935 --> 00:07:27,036
Drums, my ass.

144
00:07:28,066 --> 00:07:28,774
I brought…

145
00:07:31,209 --> 00:07:33,852
the thing!

146
00:07:34,170 --> 00:07:36,530
Damn, you’re awesome, Hem.

147
00:07:36,530 --> 00:07:38,770
We’re staying up all night tonight.

148
00:07:38,976 --> 00:07:39,631
Hell, yeah.

149
00:07:41,729 --> 00:07:42,438
Hey.

150
00:07:43,356 --> 00:07:44,927
What are you guys doing,
putting on a concert?

151
00:07:44,927 --> 00:07:46,051
Everyone else is already on the bus.

152
00:07:46,051 --> 00:07:46,713
Come on!

153
00:07:46,919 --> 00:07:47,580
What are you doing?

154
00:07:47,580 --> 00:07:48,399
The teacher is here.

155
00:07:48,586 --> 00:07:49,277
Let’s go.

156
00:07:49,521 --> 00:07:52,096
Hurry up, girls.

157
00:07:53,801 --> 00:07:56,208
- Hello.
- Hello.

158
00:07:58,437 --> 00:08:00,123
If I had to break it down…

159
00:08:00,498 --> 00:08:01,224
P’Niran.

160
00:08:01,224 --> 00:08:01,782
Huh?

161
00:08:01,782 --> 00:08:03,257
Please get up.

162
00:08:03,931 --> 00:08:06,561
Could you move over there?

163
00:08:09,315 --> 00:08:09,815
Me?

164
00:08:09,815 --> 00:08:10,470
Yes.

165
00:08:10,470 --> 00:08:11,321
Please sit here.

166
00:08:11,827 --> 00:08:12,466
Oh.

167
00:08:13,347 --> 00:08:14,236
And…

168
00:08:14,480 --> 00:08:15,356
P’Thipok.

169
00:08:15,356 --> 00:08:15,979
Yes?

170
00:08:15,979 --> 00:08:19,164
Please get up
and sit next to P’Thara.

171
00:08:22,712 --> 00:08:23,411
Please sit down.

172
00:08:24,465 --> 00:08:25,121
Yeah.

173
00:08:26,657 --> 00:08:28,575
And we’re all set.

174
00:08:28,987 --> 00:08:29,960
Cheewa, my friend.

175
00:08:31,833 --> 00:08:33,967
Feel free to take any open seat.

176
00:08:40,328 --> 00:08:41,561
You can sit here.

177
00:09:22,726 --> 00:09:24,683
Look at that big smile.

178
00:09:25,826 --> 00:09:27,706
You’ve really fallen for him, haven’t you?

179
00:09:32,952 --> 00:09:35,913
Why are you meddling, Mr. Jomyut?

180
00:09:36,456 --> 00:09:39,016
The one you just accused of meddling
is the same person

181
00:09:39,016 --> 00:09:41,345
who arranged for you to sit next to him.

182
00:09:46,562 --> 00:09:50,350
You’re very clever, Mr. Jomyut.

183
00:09:51,212 --> 00:09:54,569
You can tell, so why ask?

184
00:09:56,274 --> 00:09:57,752
Have you told him you liked him?

185
00:10:01,105 --> 00:10:02,718
I’m trying to win him over.

186
00:10:04,629 --> 00:10:05,942
If I had to guess,

187
00:10:06,635 --> 00:10:10,122
you probably stood there deadpan,
pushed up your glasses a little,

188
00:10:10,534 --> 00:10:13,525
and asked to hit on P’Niran
like a robot, right?

189
00:10:16,223 --> 00:10:19,487
What else could I do, Mr. Jomyut?

190
00:10:19,749 --> 00:10:22,192
Try to win him over the human way.

191
00:10:22,941 --> 00:10:26,400
Save your straightforwardness
for talking to the stars.

192
00:10:27,412 --> 00:10:28,465
Can you teach me how?

193
00:10:28,465 --> 00:10:29,314
I can’t.

194
00:10:30,138 --> 00:10:31,833
I’ve never hit on anyone on Earth.

195
00:10:31,833 --> 00:10:32,595
Oh?

196
00:10:33,588 --> 00:10:34,831
Look at you, giving advice.

197
00:10:35,543 --> 00:10:36,737
Talking is easier.

198
00:10:37,074 --> 00:10:37,859
Doing is hard.

199
00:10:38,889 --> 00:10:39,585
Oh?

200
00:11:01,058 --> 00:11:01,834
Hey, Niran.

201
00:11:02,939 --> 00:11:04,441
Why the hell did you bring us here?

202
00:11:04,441 --> 00:11:05,177
Yeah.

203
00:11:07,107 --> 00:11:07,797
Well…

204
00:11:21,270 --> 00:11:22,338
Come on, everyone!

205
00:11:22,621 --> 00:11:23,202
Okay.

206
00:11:23,335 --> 00:11:24,198
Alright.

207
00:11:24,564 --> 00:11:27,655
Welcome to Sea Clean Camp.

208
00:11:27,655 --> 00:11:31,265
Just a quick reminder about the school rules.

209
00:11:31,431 --> 00:11:34,417
Whatever applies there
applies here as well.

210
00:11:34,417 --> 00:11:35,823
Please behave the same way.

211
00:11:35,823 --> 00:11:36,562
One more thing.

212
00:11:36,562 --> 00:11:39,508
If anyone has anything weird or crazy,

213
00:11:39,508 --> 00:11:42,524
like illegal items, alcohol, or whatever,

214
00:11:42,524 --> 00:11:44,549
don’t let us find it. Hide it well.

215
00:11:44,549 --> 00:11:45,390
Got it?

216
00:11:45,507 --> 00:11:48,685
No. We’ll confiscate it immediately.

217
00:11:48,802 --> 00:11:51,448
- We won’t get caught. We’re slick.
- The school doesn’t allow you

218
00:11:51,448 --> 00:11:53,530
to bring illegal stuff here.

219
00:11:53,647 --> 00:11:54,536
We’ve had to deal with it every year.

220
00:11:54,536 --> 00:11:56,967
I hope we won’t have to this year.

221
00:11:57,200 --> 00:11:57,834
Okay?

222
00:11:58,034 --> 00:11:58,770
Alright.

223
00:11:58,770 --> 00:12:02,727
Enjoy yourselves, relax,
and head to your rooms.

224
00:12:02,877 --> 00:12:03,543
Let’s go.

225
00:12:04,724 --> 00:12:05,224
Come on.

226
00:12:05,807 --> 00:12:07,478
Let’s go.

227
00:12:07,478 --> 00:12:09,628
Let's go do the activity.

228
00:12:15,452 --> 00:12:16,116
Bring it.

229
00:12:16,116 --> 00:12:17,342
I exchanged a lot of money.

230
00:12:17,459 --> 00:12:18,705
I’m ready. I’m telling you.

231
00:12:18,822 --> 00:12:19,547
Good.

232
00:12:19,547 --> 00:12:20,696
You just exchanged money for me to take.

233
00:12:21,329 --> 00:12:22,914
How about 20 baht per round this time?

234
00:12:22,914 --> 00:12:24,099
Whoa, that's way too much.

235
00:12:24,099 --> 00:12:24,723
Are you trying to set yourself up for life?

236
00:12:24,723 --> 00:12:26,312
5 or 10 baht like usual is enough.

237
00:12:26,312 --> 00:12:27,650
Don't be a coward.

238
00:12:28,749 --> 00:12:30,766
Investments come with risks, you know?

239
00:12:30,766 --> 00:12:32,311
The more you put in, the more you make!

240
00:12:32,311 --> 00:12:33,065
Yeah.

241
00:12:33,448 --> 00:12:34,992
Can we join you?

242
00:12:36,374 --> 00:12:37,052
Hey.

243
00:12:37,052 --> 00:12:38,720
You two are just kids.

244
00:12:38,936 --> 00:12:40,463
Go play Ouija

245
00:12:40,627 --> 00:12:42,884
or an alien version of that.

246
00:12:43,100 --> 00:12:44,645
This game is for adults.

247
00:12:44,995 --> 00:12:46,526
I’ve watched my grandma play this
since I was a kid.

248
00:12:46,942 --> 00:12:49,133
I have experience
and I’ve memorized the techniques.

249
00:12:49,333 --> 00:12:50,135
Careful.

250
00:12:50,302 --> 00:12:52,005
You might lose to this kid and go broke.

251
00:12:52,205 --> 00:12:53,005
Whoa.

252
00:12:53,005 --> 00:12:54,179
He’s feisty.

253
00:12:54,179 --> 00:12:54,830
Look at that.

254
00:12:54,830 --> 00:12:57,093
A deck of cards has 52 cards.

255
00:12:57,093 --> 00:12:59,815
The odds of scoring a 9 are 9.65%

256
00:13:00,281 --> 00:13:01,670
Just let them join.

257
00:13:02,269 --> 00:13:03,506
I don’t want to hear theories anymore.

258
00:13:03,972 --> 00:13:05,270
I’d rather do it.

259
00:13:05,270 --> 00:13:06,276
Yeah.

260
00:13:06,276 --> 00:13:08,028
What if Teacher Boriboon finds out?

261
00:13:09,326 --> 00:13:11,529
Come on. We won’t get scolded.

262
00:13:11,662 --> 00:13:13,245
We play this at every camp, right?

263
00:13:13,245 --> 00:13:14,345
Yeah.

264
00:13:15,627 --> 00:13:16,323
Fine.

265
00:13:16,323 --> 00:13:17,461
Let’s all play together.

266
00:13:17,561 --> 00:13:18,250
Come on.

267
00:13:18,283 --> 00:13:18,965
Don’t worry.

268
00:13:19,198 --> 00:13:19,826
Come on.

269
00:13:19,826 --> 00:13:20,958
Good luck and get rich!

270
00:13:21,541 --> 00:13:22,273
Come on.

271
00:13:22,406 --> 00:13:23,233
Bring in the money.

272
00:13:23,233 --> 00:13:23,894
Come on.

273
00:13:24,327 --> 00:13:26,691
I’m going to clean you out.

274
00:13:33,426 --> 00:13:35,181
I think I like the sea breeze.

275
00:13:38,676 --> 00:13:40,304
We don’t have to go all the way down there, do we?

276
00:13:45,497 --> 00:13:46,136
Hey, Niran.

277
00:13:47,334 --> 00:13:48,917
Why the hell did you bring us here?

278
00:13:48,917 --> 00:13:49,635
Yeah.

279
00:13:51,609 --> 00:13:53,955
Well, to relax.

280
00:13:59,943 --> 00:14:04,011
Why the hell do people
throw trash into the sea?

281
00:14:05,809 --> 00:14:06,731
I know, right?

282
00:14:08,712 --> 00:14:09,641
Should we start the mission now?

283
00:14:10,627 --> 00:14:11,127
Huh?

284
00:14:11,127 --> 00:14:11,646
Yeah, let’s start cleaning up.

285
00:14:12,145 --> 00:14:14,657
Three. Two. One.

286
00:14:14,940 --> 00:14:16,411
Hey!

287
00:14:16,561 --> 00:14:17,228
Hey!

288
00:14:17,228 --> 00:14:18,389
That got in my eyes!

289
00:14:18,639 --> 00:14:19,737
Hey!

290
00:14:20,369 --> 00:14:22,553
It’s all over my face, Thara! You idiot!

291
00:14:22,823 --> 00:14:24,483
There go my shoes.

292
00:14:25,016 --> 00:14:26,162
Is that all you’ve got, Thara?

293
00:14:26,162 --> 00:14:26,990
What?

294
00:14:26,990 --> 00:14:27,599
Come on!

295
00:14:27,599 --> 00:14:28,099
Hey!

296
00:14:28,099 --> 00:14:29,809
Niran!

297
00:14:33,820 --> 00:14:34,767
What the f*ck is wrong with you, Oy?

298
00:14:34,767 --> 00:14:35,548
Why did you push me?

299
00:14:35,548 --> 00:14:36,521
Why did you kick water at me?

300
00:14:36,521 --> 00:14:37,415
When did I do that?

301
00:14:37,415 --> 00:14:38,167
Just now!

302
00:14:38,167 --> 00:14:39,136
It’s all in your head, Oy.

303
00:14:39,136 --> 00:14:40,212
I didn’t kick anything at you.

304
00:14:40,212 --> 00:14:43,848
Don’t forget you and I are at this camp
because we fought at the canteen.

305
00:14:44,431 --> 00:14:45,719
If it wasn't you, then who was it?

306
00:14:45,819 --> 00:14:46,747
Those four-eyed kids?

307
00:14:49,743 --> 00:14:51,255
My friends and I can vouch for Niran.

308
00:14:51,255 --> 00:14:52,349
He didn’t do it.

309
00:14:52,649 --> 00:14:53,783
You guys are friends.

310
00:14:53,983 --> 00:14:55,262
Of course you’re taking his side.

311
00:14:55,262 --> 00:14:57,105
Why the hell
would I get myself in more trouble?

312
00:14:57,105 --> 00:14:59,242
Shouldn’t I be the one asking you that?

313
00:14:59,641 --> 00:15:01,012
Just leave me the hell alone already.

314
00:15:01,212 --> 00:15:01,968
You’re pissing me off!

315
00:15:03,583 --> 00:15:04,218
Hey!

316
00:15:04,218 --> 00:15:04,918
Niran!

317
00:15:04,918 --> 00:15:05,418
Hey.

318
00:15:05,734 --> 00:15:06,234
Oy.

319
00:15:06,234 --> 00:15:06,977
Calm down.

320
00:15:08,924 --> 00:15:09,963
You think that’s funny?

321
00:15:10,396 --> 00:15:12,233
You think you can just walk away
after pushing me?

322
00:15:12,233 --> 00:15:13,322
Shit, Niran. I’m all soaked.

323
00:15:13,322 --> 00:15:14,265
Me too!

324
00:15:14,265 --> 00:15:15,506
Do you have eyes, you dumbass?

325
00:15:16,055 --> 00:15:16,899
Did you just insult me?

326
00:15:16,899 --> 00:15:17,822
Yes, I did!

327
00:15:18,438 --> 00:15:19,976
Your brain is only there
to keep your ears apart!

328
00:15:19,976 --> 00:15:21,168
I could keep insulting you until dark!

329
00:15:21,601 --> 00:15:22,357
Niran!

330
00:15:22,357 --> 00:15:23,049
F*ck you, Oy!

331
00:15:23,399 --> 00:15:24,113
Niran!

332
00:15:24,976 --> 00:15:25,791
Calm down.

333
00:15:26,274 --> 00:15:27,271
Niran!

334
00:15:27,704 --> 00:15:28,817
Stop it!

335
00:15:29,067 --> 00:15:29,970
Calm down!

336
00:15:29,970 --> 00:15:30,470
Stop!

337
00:15:30,470 --> 00:15:30,970
That’s enough.

338
00:15:32,551 --> 00:15:33,736
Guys, stop it.

339
00:15:37,382 --> 00:15:39,218
You guys fought
and got your behavior points deducted,

340
00:15:39,218 --> 00:15:41,397
so you had to come here to make up for it.

341
00:15:41,663 --> 00:15:42,867
And now you’re fighting again?

342
00:15:45,364 --> 00:15:46,963
Next time, you’re getting put on probation.

343
00:15:50,059 --> 00:15:51,044
Stop it already.

344
00:15:52,392 --> 00:15:53,091
Let’s go.

345
00:16:20,967 --> 00:16:22,051
What are you going to
yell at me about this time?

346
00:16:22,051 --> 00:16:22,906
Just give me the whole lecture at once.

347
00:16:23,938 --> 00:16:25,426
I know I’m being very hotheaded right now.

348
00:16:26,341 --> 00:16:27,359
Is there anything else?

349
00:16:27,875 --> 00:16:29,330
Where have you been?

350
00:16:30,062 --> 00:16:31,198
You sure picked a great time to disappear.

351
00:16:31,198 --> 00:16:31,876
If you wanted to yell at me,

352
00:16:31,876 --> 00:16:32,996
you should’ve done that when—

353
00:16:32,996 --> 00:16:33,665
Are you hurt?

354
00:16:38,276 --> 00:16:39,348
Are you hurt anywhere?

355
00:16:47,941 --> 00:16:48,972
You’re not hurt, right?

356
00:16:57,488 --> 00:16:59,491
Teacher Boriboon had me check
some documents.

357
00:16:59,491 --> 00:17:00,690
That’s why I only showed up just now.

358
00:17:05,018 --> 00:17:07,672
Why do you keep getting yourself hurt?

359
00:17:11,051 --> 00:17:12,487
I’m so worried about you, you know?

360
00:17:25,741 --> 00:17:26,881
Oy accused P’Niran.

361
00:17:29,111 --> 00:17:31,724
He said P’Niran threw water at him.

362
00:17:32,606 --> 00:17:33,476
Is he insane?

363
00:17:34,558 --> 00:17:36,424
He’s the one
who pushed P’Niran into the water first.

364
00:17:36,774 --> 00:17:37,955
He punched me first.

365
00:17:39,203 --> 00:17:40,840
I really didn’t start it this time.

366
00:17:57,414 --> 00:17:58,731
I believe you, P’Niran.

367
00:17:59,646 --> 00:18:01,211
I know you didn’t start it.

368
00:18:03,342 --> 00:18:05,699
But I still don’t like you fighting with him.

369
00:18:07,663 --> 00:18:09,039
I really don’t want you to get hurt.

370
00:18:14,445 --> 00:18:15,886
I mean it, P’Niran.

371
00:18:17,934 --> 00:18:19,751
I’m so worried about you.

372
00:18:32,410 --> 00:18:34,306
The way I’m looking at you right now

373
00:18:35,627 --> 00:18:37,122
can’t lie.

374
00:18:41,910 --> 00:18:43,214
You’re my whole world.

375
00:18:50,900 --> 00:18:52,338
I’ll protect this world.

376
00:19:11,777 --> 00:19:12,616
Why are you smiling?

377
00:19:14,131 --> 00:19:14,892
I’m not smiling.

378
00:19:22,066 --> 00:19:23,152
I’ll let it slide this time.

379
00:19:24,567 --> 00:19:26,127
Let it slide as many times as you want.

380
00:19:26,510 --> 00:19:28,080
I still insist I didn’t do it.

381
00:19:28,080 --> 00:19:29,417
If it wasn’t you, then who?

382
00:19:30,149 --> 00:19:31,755
There’s only you
and this four-eyes.

383
00:19:32,754 --> 00:19:35,553
Try using whatever little brain you have.
Who else have you been messing with?

384
00:19:35,869 --> 00:19:37,291
Why do they hate you this much?

385
00:19:37,824 --> 00:19:38,993
Just like we hate you.

386
00:19:43,088 --> 00:19:44,373
Just wait until I see you tonight!

387
00:19:46,653 --> 00:19:47,722
Of course, you’ll see me.

388
00:19:47,938 --> 00:19:48,880
Unless you’re sleeping on the street.

389
00:19:49,429 --> 00:19:50,311
You annoying asshole.

390
00:19:50,311 --> 00:19:51,234
You want me to kick your ass?

391
00:19:51,234 --> 00:19:51,873
Bring it.

392
00:19:55,818 --> 00:19:57,948
You just got in trouble for fighting.

393
00:19:58,098 --> 00:19:59,709
Now you want to get in trouble
for gambling too?

394
00:19:59,709 --> 00:20:01,195
Ghosts aren’t real.

395
00:20:01,195 --> 00:20:02,483
It’s all in your head.

396
00:20:02,916 --> 00:20:04,777
But the 12th graders last year
really saw one.

397
00:20:15,807 --> 00:20:17,430
Nine! Double payout!

398
00:20:17,430 --> 00:20:19,002
Hey!

399
00:20:19,002 --> 00:20:21,138
Lucky and rich!

400
00:20:21,359 --> 00:20:23,562
It’s not even dark yet,
but you’ve already won a lot.

401
00:20:24,541 --> 00:20:27,143
If this were real money, I’d be rich by now.

402
00:20:27,365 --> 00:20:29,356
Oh, you guys aren’t playing with real money?

403
00:20:30,604 --> 00:20:31,275
No.

404
00:20:31,512 --> 00:20:32,506
We just pretend we are.

405
00:20:33,359 --> 00:20:34,456
We just count how much we win.

406
00:20:34,456 --> 00:20:36,545
Whoever wins the most
gets to punish whoever wins the least.

407
00:20:36,545 --> 00:20:37,867
Such babies.

408
00:20:39,367 --> 00:20:40,746
Did you just insult me, nerd?

409
00:20:42,009 --> 00:20:42,866
Throw him.

410
00:20:44,540 --> 00:20:46,306
You just got in trouble for fighting.

411
00:20:46,638 --> 00:20:48,114
Now you want to get in trouble
for gambling too?

412
00:20:48,777 --> 00:20:49,963
Damn.

413
00:20:50,503 --> 00:20:51,215
Where’d he come from?

414
00:20:51,972 --> 00:20:53,576
You’re all such babies here.

415
00:20:54,113 --> 00:20:54,870
It’s disappointing.

416
00:20:55,470 --> 00:20:56,840
You don’t even dare to play for real money.

417
00:20:57,440 --> 00:20:58,519
Oh, this guy.

418
00:21:05,628 --> 00:21:07,197
Come on. Let’s go eat.

419
00:21:08,144 --> 00:21:08,867
Let’s go eat.

420
00:21:11,962 --> 00:21:13,061
Stop making that face.

421
00:21:13,629 --> 00:21:14,572
It’s like Suchart is at this camp with us.

422
00:21:15,882 --> 00:21:16,897
Let’s put this away, guys.

423
00:21:16,897 --> 00:21:17,578
Come on.

424
00:21:17,578 --> 00:21:19,135
Let’s come back and play this properly later.

425
00:21:19,135 --> 00:21:20,481
Show the kids how it’s done.

426
00:21:20,481 --> 00:21:21,229
Yeah.

427
00:21:21,418 --> 00:21:22,606
Prepare a lot of money.

428
00:21:24,011 --> 00:21:24,651
What was that?

429
00:21:25,093 --> 00:21:25,641
Let’s go.

430
00:21:27,267 --> 00:21:27,829
Hide it.

431
00:21:32,582 --> 00:21:33,883
Ghosts aren’t real.

432
00:21:34,183 --> 00:21:35,133
It’s all in your head.

433
00:21:35,907 --> 00:21:37,594
But the 12th graders last year
really saw one.

434
00:21:38,605 --> 00:21:39,777
We should take that with a grain of salt.

435
00:21:40,219 --> 00:21:41,670
They were exaggerating like crazy.

436
00:21:42,570 --> 00:21:43,890
I don’t know if it was an exaggeration,

437
00:21:44,253 --> 00:21:45,897
but Niran slept with the lights on
for like a month.

438
00:21:46,008 --> 00:21:47,612
Not true. I always turned the lights off.

439
00:21:47,786 --> 00:21:49,943
If anyone sees a ghost tonight,
I’ll treat them to a meal.

440
00:21:50,195 --> 00:21:52,388
I’ll split the bill with Cheewa and Newton.

441
00:21:52,688 --> 00:21:54,158
What? Why?

442
00:21:54,158 --> 00:21:54,976
Here’s some water.

443
00:21:56,523 --> 00:21:58,103
Wow, Cheewa.

444
00:21:58,482 --> 00:22:00,150
We’re all sitting right here.

445
00:22:00,497 --> 00:22:02,955
I guess I’m invisible to you.

446
00:22:04,313 --> 00:22:06,018
I’m thirsty too.

447
00:22:06,350 --> 00:22:07,963
I can get you a new one.

448
00:22:08,737 --> 00:22:10,236
Please take this one.

449
00:22:14,736 --> 00:22:15,605
Look at that chemistry.

450
00:22:15,794 --> 00:22:16,918
You just noticed?

451
00:22:19,539 --> 00:22:21,314
Hey, while on the bus,

452
00:22:21,646 --> 00:22:23,510
I saw you sleeping on his shoulder.

453
00:22:25,692 --> 00:22:26,770
You just saw that?

454
00:22:28,949 --> 00:22:30,175
Don’t pressure him, guys.

455
00:22:31,186 --> 00:22:33,405
By the way, is he really hitting on you?

456
00:22:35,692 --> 00:22:37,726
Wait, you just found out too?

457
00:22:38,626 --> 00:22:39,430
Shut up.

458
00:22:39,825 --> 00:22:41,254
I was just asking my friend.

459
00:22:42,217 --> 00:22:43,554
You guys are the worst.

460
00:22:44,312 --> 00:22:46,617
We have to prepare for the campfire activity.

461
00:22:47,012 --> 00:22:48,009
Damn!

462
00:22:49,683 --> 00:22:50,987
I got chills.

463
00:22:51,729 --> 00:22:52,293
Whoa.

464
00:22:52,767 --> 00:22:54,455
What’s the activity?

465
00:22:57,123 --> 00:23:00,177
Teacher Boriboon asked us to form a group and put on a skit about the stars.

466
00:23:01,488 --> 00:23:02,762
I’m playing Planet Namek.

467
00:23:03,315 --> 00:23:04,014
Dumbass.

468
00:23:04,188 --> 00:23:05,529
Planet Namek isn’t real.

469
00:23:05,987 --> 00:23:07,193
Wait, it isn’t real, is it?

470
00:23:07,193 --> 00:23:08,333
No, it’s not real.

471
00:23:09,044 --> 00:23:10,131
You two decide.

472
00:23:12,752 --> 00:23:14,883
We have to choose stars
that are related to each other

473
00:23:15,451 --> 00:23:17,712
so the story flows.

474
00:23:18,644 --> 00:23:19,206
Whoa.

475
00:23:19,443 --> 00:23:21,570
I only know the Moon star, Mars, and Mercury.

476
00:23:21,933 --> 00:23:23,276
There’s no such thing as a Moon star.

477
00:23:23,671 --> 00:23:24,817
I’m just rambling.

478
00:23:27,580 --> 00:23:29,253
What star do you want to play?

479
00:23:32,127 --> 00:23:32,936
Wow.

480
00:23:33,599 --> 00:23:34,962
Are there any cool stars?

481
00:23:35,692 --> 00:23:36,518
Can you choose one for me?

482
00:23:36,944 --> 00:23:38,809
Maybe that star you were talking about
this morning.

483
00:23:39,693 --> 00:23:41,539
Do you want to be Scorpius?

484
00:23:43,134 --> 00:23:44,964
Any other stars?

485
00:23:45,327 --> 00:23:46,879
Which star do you think suits me?

486
00:23:55,589 --> 00:23:57,632
No need to take it that seriously.

487
00:23:58,074 --> 00:24:00,146
Teacher Boriboon just wants us
to have fun with it.

488
00:24:00,146 --> 00:24:02,208
He’s not looking for new directors.

489
00:24:03,045 --> 00:24:05,412
I’m just thinking about
which star you’re like.

490
00:24:07,007 --> 00:24:08,140
And which star are you like?

491
00:24:10,935 --> 00:24:12,888
I think I’m like…

492
00:24:14,041 --> 00:24:14,798
Saturn.

493
00:24:15,098 --> 00:24:16,067
Wait, wait, wait.

494
00:24:16,367 --> 00:24:17,338
I know that one.

495
00:24:17,338 --> 00:24:19,011
Saturn has rings.

496
00:24:19,469 --> 00:24:20,467
It’s so cool.

497
00:24:20,467 --> 00:24:22,037
Are there any other stars with rings?

498
00:24:24,248 --> 00:24:24,915
Are there?

499
00:24:26,604 --> 00:24:27,466
The Moon star.

500
00:24:27,608 --> 00:24:28,728
It’s the Moon.

501
00:24:29,375 --> 00:24:30,394
Yeah, there’s no such thing as a Moon star.

502
00:24:30,394 --> 00:24:31,673
Neptune.

503
00:24:31,673 --> 00:24:33,142
That’s so cool.

504
00:24:33,221 --> 00:24:35,074
But Planet Namek is real, you know?

505
00:24:36,100 --> 00:24:37,144
I’m serious.

506
00:24:37,870 --> 00:24:39,992
I’ve read about it on social media.

507
00:24:40,071 --> 00:24:41,605
Can you dye your hair blond?

508
00:24:41,605 --> 00:24:42,173
Huh?

509
00:24:42,173 --> 00:24:43,543
Dye your hair blond and show me.

510
00:24:45,567 --> 00:24:48,330
No. The Sun has to speak first.

511
00:24:48,614 --> 00:24:49,284
Go ahead.

512
00:24:49,284 --> 00:24:49,804
Oh?

513
00:24:52,315 --> 00:24:54,607
By the power of the universe,

514
00:24:55,128 --> 00:24:57,151
today, I shall judge…

515
00:24:57,625 --> 00:24:58,290
The comet!

516
00:25:01,669 --> 00:25:02,627
No.

517
00:25:03,022 --> 00:25:04,200
You’re the Sun.

518
00:25:04,200 --> 00:25:05,219
You have to speak more firmly.

519
00:25:05,834 --> 00:25:06,345
Oh?

520
00:25:09,882 --> 00:25:10,935
I was wrong,

521
00:25:11,282 --> 00:25:12,350
Lord Sun!

522
00:25:14,845 --> 00:25:15,698
Alright.

523
00:25:16,077 --> 00:25:17,161
Uncle Jupiter can speak now,

524
00:25:17,493 --> 00:25:18,297
as the witness.

525
00:25:19,765 --> 00:25:21,166
Ugh.

526
00:25:21,403 --> 00:25:23,670
I’m busy raising my children
and grandchildren,

527
00:25:24,538 --> 00:25:28,154
and then this comet suddenly comes flying in
to cause trouble.

528
00:25:28,833 --> 00:25:30,974
Everything got damaged.

529
00:25:31,464 --> 00:25:32,042
Oh!

530
00:25:33,084 --> 00:25:37,967
My nearly a hundred children and  grandchildren
were all scared.

531
00:25:41,496 --> 00:25:43,172
Are you just making this up, Uncle?

532
00:25:43,709 --> 00:25:45,096
You have like a hundred children
and grandchildren?

533
00:25:46,075 --> 00:25:50,152
Well, Cheewa said
Jupiter has over a hundred moons.

534
00:25:50,152 --> 00:25:50,692
Is that not right?

535
00:25:50,692 --> 00:25:52,340
No, that's not in the script.

536
00:25:52,340 --> 00:25:52,840
Hey!

537
00:25:57,418 --> 00:25:58,370
Keep rehearsing.

538
00:25:58,986 --> 00:26:00,030
Earth, speak now.

539
00:26:00,251 --> 00:26:01,662
No, I mean,

540
00:26:01,836 --> 00:26:03,257
Mr. Cheewa, please speak now.

541
00:26:06,241 --> 00:26:08,174
There are several million stars
in the universe.

542
00:26:09,121 --> 00:26:10,498
Why do I have to be Earth?

543
00:26:11,240 --> 00:26:13,022
Oh? What's wrong with Earth?

544
00:26:16,354 --> 00:26:18,363
I already made you my world.

545
00:26:19,279 --> 00:26:20,726
You’re my world.

546
00:26:25,336 --> 00:26:27,224
Can I be the narrator instead?

547
00:26:27,729 --> 00:26:28,461
I don’t want to act.

548
00:26:29,787 --> 00:26:31,019
Mr. Cheewa’s getting whiny.

549
00:26:31,966 --> 00:26:34,445
Just play along and make it perfect.

550
00:26:36,813 --> 00:26:38,363
Come on, don’t argue.

551
00:26:39,121 --> 00:26:40,600
If Cheewa doesn’t want to act,

552
00:26:40,837 --> 00:26:41,909
let him narrate.

553
00:26:42,004 --> 00:26:43,365
That way, he won’t have to do anything silly.

554
00:26:43,365 --> 00:26:44,364
What do you mean, silly?

555
00:26:46,069 --> 00:26:47,632
The universe is never silly.

556
00:26:48,295 --> 00:26:49,119
You’re in trouble, Hem.

557
00:26:50,824 --> 00:26:52,300
I’m just kidding.

558
00:26:52,647 --> 00:26:54,201
Don’t take it seriously, nerd.

559
00:26:55,433 --> 00:26:57,732
Over the course of 13.8 billion years of history,

560
00:26:57,732 --> 00:26:59,429
no one has ever said the universe is silly.

561
00:27:01,703 --> 00:27:03,652
Yeah, Hem.

562
00:27:03,652 --> 00:27:04,725
This is all on you.

563
00:27:04,914 --> 00:27:06,887
How could you insult the universe?

564
00:27:07,440 --> 00:27:08,642
Apologize now.

565
00:27:09,321 --> 00:27:10,264
I was wrong.

566
00:27:10,692 --> 00:27:12,766
Universe, I’m sorry.

567
00:27:12,766 --> 00:27:14,744
Yeah, keep apologizing.

568
00:27:17,097 --> 00:27:19,693
Oh, I’ve never seen Hem like this before.

569
00:27:20,925 --> 00:27:21,620
He’s lost it.

570
00:27:24,004 --> 00:27:25,153
Oh, you’re not going to answer me.

571
00:27:29,000 --> 00:27:30,003
Leave us alone!

572
00:27:40,571 --> 00:27:41,381
I think it’s here.

573
00:27:47,050 --> 00:27:47,819
Here it is.

574
00:27:50,330 --> 00:27:51,121
Hurry. Let’s go!

575
00:27:52,384 --> 00:27:52,963
Let’s go.

576
00:27:58,275 --> 00:27:59,586
Why are you blocking us, four-eyes?

577
00:28:00,107 --> 00:28:01,693
Why are you two doing this?

578
00:28:02,025 --> 00:28:03,249
You’re on the student council.

579
00:28:03,470 --> 00:28:04,878
You should be on our side.

580
00:28:05,194 --> 00:28:07,532
We’re about to report this contraband
to the teachers.

581
00:28:18,442 --> 00:28:22,449
But because that star is
running out of energy,

582
00:28:22,897 --> 00:28:25,699
it collapses

583
00:28:25,955 --> 00:28:28,185
and causes a massive explosion.

584
00:28:28,377 --> 00:28:31,230
Supernova!

585
00:28:40,400 --> 00:28:42,284
Come on, clap!

586
00:28:51,540 --> 00:28:53,888
There’s no one else to play the role,
so I had to fill in.

587
00:28:53,888 --> 00:28:54,986
I’m so embarrassed. I’m going crazy.

588
00:28:54,986 --> 00:28:56,009
Next group, hurry up and take over.

589
00:28:56,009 --> 00:28:57,000
I’m so embarrassed.

590
00:28:57,000 --> 00:28:59,585
Come on, let’s clap for the next group.

591
00:29:00,455 --> 00:29:01,839
Put those away.

592
00:29:01,839 --> 00:29:03,098
Come on.

593
00:29:03,311 --> 00:29:04,058
Backs to them first.

594
00:29:04,058 --> 00:29:04,703
Backs to them.

595
00:29:05,023 --> 00:29:06,335
Go ahead.

596
00:29:06,769 --> 00:29:07,795
Let’s walk with our backs to them.

597
00:29:07,795 --> 00:29:08,452
Don’t turn around yet.

598
00:29:09,710 --> 00:29:11,921
As if I couldn't tell who you are.

599
00:29:20,132 --> 00:29:22,044
Three. Two. One.

600
00:29:22,172 --> 00:29:23,197
Turn left.

601
00:29:29,413 --> 00:29:30,544
Come on, let’s do it!

602
00:29:32,037 --> 00:29:32,958
Come on!

603
00:29:43,823 --> 00:29:47,272
Ugh, Comet, what have you done?

604
00:29:47,592 --> 00:29:50,032
You scared all my children
and grandchildren!

605
00:29:52,634 --> 00:29:53,848
Come on, Uncle.

606
00:29:53,848 --> 00:29:54,643
I’m a comet.

607
00:29:54,643 --> 00:29:56,209
I’m meant to blast off.

608
00:29:56,209 --> 00:29:56,709
Stop.

609
00:29:56,709 --> 00:29:58,198
How am I supposed to slow down?

610
00:29:58,198 --> 00:29:59,164
No one else is complaining around here.

611
00:29:59,313 --> 00:30:00,365
Right, Earth?

612
00:30:07,147 --> 00:30:07,873
Ugh!

613
00:30:13,376 --> 00:30:15,628
This auntie’s complained so much,
she doesn’t know what else to say anymore!

614
00:30:16,353 --> 00:30:18,288
You teenage comet!

615
00:30:23,682 --> 00:30:25,055
I’m Auntie Earth, you know!

616
00:30:29,342 --> 00:30:32,721
The home of who-knows-how-many species of living things.

617
00:30:37,178 --> 00:30:39,015
If you crash into me,

618
00:30:41,233 --> 00:30:43,746
where are all the living things in my house
supposed to go?

619
00:30:51,172 --> 00:30:53,360
I’m taking this case to the Sun Court!

620
00:30:54,618 --> 00:30:55,477
Just you wait!

621
00:30:55,477 --> 00:30:57,503
Yeah, I’m not scared!

622
00:30:57,503 --> 00:30:59,341
If you’ve got the guts,
go complain to the Sun Court!

623
00:31:00,279 --> 00:31:03,462
By the power of the Universe Court,

624
00:31:03,782 --> 00:31:05,986
I shall judge today.

625
00:31:07,884 --> 00:31:09,507
I was wrong.

626
00:31:10,317 --> 00:31:12,261
I can’t.

627
00:31:21,197 --> 00:31:22,181
That was exhausting.

628
00:31:22,181 --> 00:31:23,308
Whose idea was this?

629
00:31:30,373 --> 00:31:32,568
Go back to your rooms.

630
00:31:35,469 --> 00:31:36,284
Aren’t you coming?

631
00:31:36,284 --> 00:31:37,121
You go ahead.

632
00:31:37,121 --> 00:31:37,692
I’ll catch up with you later.

633
00:31:37,692 --> 00:31:38,380
Okay.

634
00:31:38,380 --> 00:31:40,663
Take the stuff and follow your friends.

635
00:31:41,303 --> 00:31:43,209
Hurry back to your rooms.

636
00:31:47,470 --> 00:31:48,748
Why are you blocking us, four-eyes?

637
00:31:49,601 --> 00:31:51,460
Why are you two doing this?

638
00:31:54,361 --> 00:31:55,048
Why not?

639
00:31:55,325 --> 00:31:56,703
You’re on the student council.

640
00:31:56,874 --> 00:31:58,287
You should be on our side.

641
00:31:58,607 --> 00:32:01,332
We’re about to report this contraband
to the teachers.

642
00:32:01,951 --> 00:32:03,237
Why are you doing this?

643
00:32:03,941 --> 00:32:06,685
Don’t you believe P’Niran
when he said he didn’t bully you?

644
00:32:08,796 --> 00:32:09,731
I don’t believe that.

645
00:32:13,143 --> 00:32:14,747
You’re just going to report it to the teacher, right?

646
00:32:15,941 --> 00:32:17,971
Will that alone satisfy you?

647
00:32:27,460 --> 00:32:30,111
Are you seriously going to let him
take our cards like that?

648
00:32:32,862 --> 00:32:34,224
When did he even take them?

649
00:32:34,373 --> 00:32:35,126
No idea.

650
00:32:35,126 --> 00:32:36,794
They were on my bed the whole time.

651
00:32:37,413 --> 00:32:38,735
And he was downstairs with us.

652
00:32:39,793 --> 00:32:40,460
Yeah.

653
00:32:41,228 --> 00:32:42,990
Your friend is taking his student council role
a little too seriously, don’t you think?

654
00:32:44,248 --> 00:32:47,418
You guys are our seniors.
Pull rank and make him give the cards back.

655
00:32:48,143 --> 00:32:50,402
How could you let Cheewa take them
and go to sleep like that?

656
00:32:51,724 --> 00:32:53,148
He’s your friend.

657
00:32:53,447 --> 00:32:54,443
You go get them back.

658
00:32:55,339 --> 00:32:56,023
Yeah.

659
00:32:57,025 --> 00:32:58,322
Just try asking him.

660
00:32:58,770 --> 00:33:00,174
We’re not playing for money.

661
00:33:01,774 --> 00:33:02,575
You guys are like triplets.

662
00:33:02,575 --> 00:33:03,276
You go.

663
00:33:03,276 --> 00:33:04,568
He won’t believe us.

664
00:33:05,165 --> 00:33:07,165
Just try asking him.

665
00:33:07,272 --> 00:33:08,815
Get the cards back.

666
00:33:10,948 --> 00:33:11,564
What?

667
00:33:11,799 --> 00:33:13,231
You try asking him.

668
00:33:13,594 --> 00:33:14,345
Why me?

669
00:33:14,516 --> 00:33:15,441
To get the cards back to us.

670
00:33:15,441 --> 00:33:16,467
Did you really have to ask?

671
00:33:16,467 --> 00:33:17,117
Go.

672
00:33:17,117 --> 00:33:17,783
Come on, go.

673
00:33:19,767 --> 00:33:20,771
Shit!

674
00:33:23,479 --> 00:33:24,591
Ouch!

675
00:33:24,591 --> 00:33:25,740
Sorry, my friend’s old.

676
00:33:32,252 --> 00:33:32,966
Cheewa.

677
00:33:34,267 --> 00:33:35,157
Cheewa, have you fallen asleep?

678
00:33:36,245 --> 00:33:37,455
I’m not giving them back.

679
00:33:45,856 --> 00:33:46,588
Beg him.

680
00:33:46,588 --> 00:33:47,216
Please.

681
00:33:47,216 --> 00:33:49,682
We rarely get to hang out and play like this.

682
00:33:50,450 --> 00:33:51,314
No.

683
00:33:51,655 --> 00:33:52,724
You don’t want the teachers to see them.

684
00:33:56,200 --> 00:33:59,014
If no one tells the teachers,
how would they know where they are?

685
00:34:11,704 --> 00:34:13,646
P’Niran, please trust me for once.

686
00:34:18,276 --> 00:34:19,029
What now?

687
00:34:22,740 --> 00:34:23,430
Hey.

688
00:34:23,771 --> 00:34:26,121
I’ve been told some of you brought cards.

689
00:34:28,360 --> 00:34:29,169
I did.

690
00:34:41,572 --> 00:34:44,161
You’re on the student council, Cheewa.

691
00:34:44,161 --> 00:34:45,996
Why did you break the rules yourself?

692
00:34:46,998 --> 00:34:49,972
I can’t believe
you brought something like this.

693
00:34:51,102 --> 00:34:52,494
I’m sorry.

694
00:34:56,994 --> 00:34:58,293
Is there anything you want to tell me?

695
00:35:00,982 --> 00:35:01,940
No.

696
00:35:02,580 --> 00:35:05,070
Please punish me however you see fit.

697
00:35:24,847 --> 00:35:26,088
Why the hell did you tell the teacher?

698
00:35:26,813 --> 00:35:27,459
Hey!

699
00:35:27,993 --> 00:35:28,663
I didn’t do it.

700
00:35:30,113 --> 00:35:31,562
Are you saying you didn’t tell the teacher?

701
00:35:31,733 --> 00:35:32,631
I’d be stupid to believe that.

702
00:35:32,802 --> 00:35:33,796
I didn’t do it.

703
00:35:34,244 --> 00:35:35,767
Just like you kept saying you didn’t do it.

704
00:35:38,028 --> 00:35:39,501
Whether you believe me or not is up to you.

705
00:35:48,135 --> 00:35:49,373
I was the one who told the teacher.

706
00:35:53,361 --> 00:35:54,308
Why would you do that?

707
00:35:55,822 --> 00:35:57,279
I don’t like breaking the rules.

708
00:35:59,070 --> 00:36:01,441
And I don’t want you and your friends
to get in trouble.

709
00:36:05,088 --> 00:36:06,764
I’m not joking, P’Niran.

710
00:36:06,982 --> 00:36:08,354
I’m really worried about you.

711
00:36:09,122 --> 00:36:11,385
You can’t afford to have any more
behavior points deducted.

712
00:36:16,482 --> 00:36:19,040
So what did the teacher say?

713
00:36:20,640 --> 00:36:23,679
He asked me to pick up 100 pieces of trash
as punishment.

714
00:36:23,871 --> 00:36:24,840
Right now?

715
00:36:25,395 --> 00:36:26,338
Right now.

716
00:36:26,850 --> 00:36:30,154
The Astronomy Club members
are going stargazing.

717
00:36:31,412 --> 00:36:34,933
But… do you want to come with me?

718
00:36:45,020 --> 00:36:46,683
The 99th one.

719
00:36:46,683 --> 00:36:49,429
By the time you finish picking up the trash,
all the stars will probably be gone.

720
00:36:50,645 --> 00:36:51,579
Did you know?

721
00:36:52,006 --> 00:36:53,919
The stars are always in the same place.

722
00:36:54,559 --> 00:36:56,995
We just need to take ourselves
somewhere we can see them.

723
00:36:59,021 --> 00:36:59,953
Where are they?

724
00:37:00,678 --> 00:37:01,762
Follow me.

725
00:37:21,631 --> 00:37:22,547
Wow.

726
00:37:22,995 --> 00:37:24,636
There are way more stars here
than at school.

727
00:37:26,598 --> 00:37:28,082
Because it’s really dark here.

728
00:37:33,926 --> 00:37:34,582
Hey.

729
00:37:35,627 --> 00:37:36,722
Tell me more.

730
00:37:36,982 --> 00:37:38,827
Why do you think you’re like Saturn?

731
00:37:41,301 --> 00:37:43,016
My personality is like Saturn’s.

732
00:37:43,933 --> 00:37:45,299
Saturn is organized.

733
00:37:45,576 --> 00:37:47,050
He does things step-by-step

734
00:37:47,285 --> 00:37:48,407
and thinks systematically.

735
00:37:52,523 --> 00:37:55,513
Are you so close to Saturn
that you know what its personality is like?

736
00:37:55,833 --> 00:37:56,654
Yes.

737
00:37:57,209 --> 00:38:00,696
I’m closer to the universe
than I am to people.

738
00:38:13,450 --> 00:38:17,276
Did you know
what star you’d be if you were one?

739
00:38:19,259 --> 00:38:20,668
You don’t want me to be your world anymore?

740
00:38:28,670 --> 00:38:29,563
Well…

741
00:38:30,182 --> 00:38:31,120
What star am I like?

742
00:38:35,322 --> 00:38:36,235
The North Star.

743
00:38:37,963 --> 00:38:38,696
Why?

744
00:38:39,080 --> 00:38:41,875
Is the North Star
a burned-out judo athlete like me?

745
00:38:43,751 --> 00:38:45,601
It’s not exactly burned out.

746
00:38:47,414 --> 00:38:49,760
The North Star is pretty hard to spot.

747
00:38:51,039 --> 00:38:54,830
Its position looks different
depending on where you are.

748
00:38:57,027 --> 00:38:59,596
You also have to take the latitude of
your location into account.

749
00:39:00,982 --> 00:39:03,113
If we’re looking from here…

750
00:39:11,088 --> 00:39:14,415
I thought the North Star
would be brighter than the rest.

751
00:39:16,868 --> 00:39:18,216
There are many factors.

752
00:39:20,626 --> 00:39:25,402
But if you ask
whether the North Star is actually bright,

753
00:39:26,660 --> 00:39:29,854
I still think it is.

754
00:39:38,207 --> 00:39:39,432
Did you know?

755
00:39:40,541 --> 00:39:42,629
The North Star never falls.

756
00:39:43,887 --> 00:39:45,128
It’s always in the same place.

757
00:39:46,130 --> 00:39:49,843
It’s even brighter than the Sun,
and it’s huge too.

758
00:39:50,504 --> 00:39:51,251
Really?

759
00:39:51,507 --> 00:39:53,282
But from where you pointed it out to me,

760
00:39:53,815 --> 00:39:55,447
it doesn’t look that bright.

761
00:39:58,006 --> 00:40:02,876
It’s because Earth and the North Star
are farther apart than you can imagine.

762
00:40:08,421 --> 00:40:10,982
But the North Star isn’t a lonely star.

763
00:40:12,982 --> 00:40:14,816
Even though we can’t see it from here,

764
00:40:15,840 --> 00:40:17,262
it has friends.

765
00:40:18,840 --> 00:40:20,157
It’s not alone.

766
00:40:24,982 --> 00:40:28,612
To me, you’re like the North Star.

767
00:40:31,342 --> 00:40:35,975
Both beautiful and meaningful.

768
00:40:51,627 --> 00:40:53,356
I like the North Star
more than anything in the world.

769
00:40:54,593 --> 00:40:56,978
♪ Do you know?

770
00:40:56,978 --> 00:41:00,047
♪ Love needs no reason ♪

771
00:41:00,047 --> 00:41:04,511
♪ It needs no definition ♪

772
00:41:04,511 --> 00:41:10,150
♪ As long as we share the same vision ♪

773
00:41:10,150 --> 00:41:11,697
I want to go to school with you for a change.

774
00:41:11,825 --> 00:41:13,211
You can’t walk with me, kid.

775
00:41:13,211 --> 00:41:15,368
Our color teams are direct rivals.

776
00:41:15,688 --> 00:41:16,442
Cheewa,

777
00:41:16,741 --> 00:41:17,758
your glasses are broken.

778
00:41:18,077 --> 00:41:20,479
You look pretty handsome without your glasses.

779
00:41:20,671 --> 00:41:22,500
Please take care of him, P’Niran.

780
00:41:22,692 --> 00:41:24,856
Thank you so much for seeing me home.

781
00:41:24,856 --> 00:41:28,214
This is the first time
Cheewa has brought a friend home.

782
00:41:28,214 --> 00:41:29,358
Do you want to play a game?

783
00:41:29,358 --> 00:41:32,277
If you lose,
you’d better not cry like a baby.

784
00:41:32,725 --> 00:41:34,774
Can you see when we’re this close?

785
00:41:36,139 --> 00:41:37,236
How about this close?
